---
Scope reviewed: internal/services/accounts/projection.go, internal/services/accounts/projection_test.go
(staged, uncommitted, matches .swarm/manifests/R12.3.files), .swarm/tier3/R12/report.md,
.swarm/tier3/R12/oracle/zz_oracle_r12_test.go.

METHOD: all probing done in a scratch copy under
/tmp/.../scratchpad/r12check (git archive of HEAD + `git diff --cached` applied), never in
the working tree, and deleted afterward. No file was left in the repo or any worktree.

PRIME TARGET A (oracle correctness) — CONFIRMED SOUND.
- Check 4's corrected fixture (day+10, not day+5): traced the arithmetic by hand and by
  execution. asOfDay=nowUTCDay, occ=+10, horizonEnd=+35. Advance loop leaves occ at +10
  (already After asOfDay). Apply loop applies +10 (<=35) then advances to +40, which is
  >35 and excluded. One occurrence of 600 applies -> minimum 400. Matches the assertion.
  Second occurrence correctly falls OUTSIDE the window now (was inside before the fix,
  confirmed by re-running the pre-correction fixture: 0 relevant regression here).
- Checks 1-3 hand-traced similarly (Check 1's cross-zone invariant, Check 2's same-UTC-day
  BalanceAt inclusion, Check 3's next-UTC-day occurrence) — no arithmetic error found in
  any of the four checks against the CURRENT code.

PRIME TARGET B (the third/fourth cutoff) — REAL DEFECT FOUND.
Enumerated every day-boundary in Project: BalanceAt's `at` cutoff, asOfDay, horizonEnd,
each occurrence label (write), each walk label (read), the reported Crossing date,
medianInboundPairedTransfer/thresholdFor (neither is date-sensitive, confirmed by
reading — no boundary there). All six are correctly UTC-normalized in the CURRENT code:
asOfUTC := asOf.UTC() feeds BalanceAt, asOfDay, and (via .UTC()) every occurrence; Crossing
is built from asOfDay, which carries UTC location.

However, per the task's own named attack ("pass asOf rather than asOfUTC to BalanceAt.
Does a committed test catch each?"), I mutated projection.go line 108 in the scratch copy:

    start, err := BalanceAt(acct, txs, asOfUTC)   ->   start, err := BalanceAt(acct, txs, asOf)

This exactly reintroduces the third defect the lead's own Tier-3 oracle was written to
catch (report.md: "3. Normalising only the grid left BalanceAt's cutoff in asOf's own
Location, dropping an already-posted transaction from the starting balance").

Result: with this mutation applied, `go test ./internal/services/accounts/...` (the
PERSISTED suite, i.e. projection_test.go plus the package's other tests) reports
0 FAILures out of 57 PASS. Re-verified with `-run TestProject -v` and with the full
package run twice. The same mutation, with the Tier-3 oracle file
(.swarm/tier3/R12/oracle/zz_oracle_r12_test.go) copied in, correctly fails 3 of its 4
checks (TestZZOracleR12_OutputDependsOnlyOnTheUTCInstant,
TestZZOracleR12_StartingBalanceUsesTheUTCDay, TestZZOracleR12_TimeNowDerivedAsOfAppliesRecurring)
— so the mutation is real and detectable, just not by anything that survives after the
oracle is deleted.

I grepped projection_test.go for any test exercising "a transaction posted on asOf's own
UTC day, in a positive-offset zone, must be included in the starting balance" (the
scenario oracle Check 2 pins) — none exists. The four new R12-attempt-3 tests
(TestProject_SameUTCDayOccurrenceNotDoubleApplied,
TestProject_MonthlyCrossingIsNotOneCycleLateAcrossZones,
TestProject_NegativeOffsetZoneAppliesOccurrence,
TestProject_TimeNowDerivedAsOfAppliesRecurring_FixedInterval) all exercise the
occurrence-label/walk-agreement defect (attempt 2's bug); none exercises the
BalanceAt-cutoff defect (the newest one, found only by the Tier-3 oracle after attempt 2's
own code was merged as HEAD). Confirmed via `git show HEAD:...projection.go` that HEAD
(the last committed state) has the un-normalized `BalanceAt(acct, txs, asOf)` -- i.e. this
exact fix is new to this attempt and is exactly the kind of change the brief says needs a
persisted test ("every one demonstrated by a test persisted in the tree").

A second named mutation -- `asOfDay := dayOf(asOfUTC)` -> `dayOf(asOf)` -- IS caught (1
FAIL in the persisted suite), so the gap is specific to the BalanceAt call, not systemic.

CONSEQUENCE: R12 has now failed for a THIRD distinct reason across three attempts, each
found by mutating exactly the line the previous attempt fixed and discovering no
persisted test protects it. The oracle (deleted after acceptance per its own header
comment) is the only thing currently standing between this code and a silent
reintroduction of "an already-posted transaction dropped from the starting balance" --
the exact user-facing bug the Tier-3 process was convened to fix. That is not
demonstrated to be fixed for the future; it is demonstrated to be fixed for right now.

OTHER ATTACKS RUN, ALL CLEAN (no findings):
- Crossing's Location: built from asOfDay (asOf.UTC()-derived), always UTC across all
  five zones. Verified via TestZZOracleR12_OutputDependsOnlyOnTheUTCInstant and my own
  probe.
- out.AsOf echoes the caller's original asOf unchanged (by design, documented at
  projection.go:96-98); not itself a defect.
- DST: constructed asOf = 2026-10-10 09:00 America/New_York (window spans the Nov 1 2026
  fall-back transition). Occurrence at UTC-day 35 applied, at UTC-day 36 excluded, in
  UTC/America/New_York/Asia/Tokyo/Pacific/Midway alike -- the 35-day window is pure UTC
  calendar arithmetic with no local-clock involvement, so DST cannot skip or double a day.
- Occurrence exactly on asOf's UTC instant and one second after UTC midnight: both behave
  per the documented asOfDay+1 contract (verified with a standalone probe: exact-instant
  occurrence skipped for that date, next occurrence in the series still applied; one-
  second-after-midnight applied).
- Negative-offset zone (Pacific/Midway) and DST-crossing zone (America/New_York): no day
  gain/loss observed in either.
- Dashboard/MCP parity (TestDashboardAndMCPProjectionAgree) and R5's
  TestGetBalanceProjectionDefaultAsOf* tests: run under TZ=Asia/Tokyo, all PASS.
- `go build ./...`, `go vet ./...` clean in the real repo.
- R1/R3/R5/R7/R10/R13 accepted tests: ledger.tsv confirms all `accepted`;
  `go test -race ./internal/services/mcpsvc/ledger/... ./internal/handlers/dashboard/...
  ./internal/services/accounts/...` all PASS.

No probe file or scratch artifact was left in the repo, any worktree, or the shared
